# ------------------------------------------------------ the shell's search

[break] a-link-in-a-root-that-leads-out-taken
rule: A program reached through a link inside an avoided root is passed over, wherever the link leads: the link can be replaced after the harness chose it.
file: crates/cineris-base/src/program.rs
in: passes_through
find: .chain(std::iter::once(&real))
replace: .skip(usize::MAX).chain(std::iter::once(&real))
packages: cineris-base
caught-by:
    cineris-base program::tests::a_link_into_or_out_of_an_avoided_root_is_passed_over

[break] a-link-only-followed-to-its-end
rule: A link outside the roots that leads through a link inside one, and out again, is passed over: each link on the way is a place a command could change.
file: crates/cineris-base/src/program.rs
in: places_on_the_way
find: places.push(directory.join(&name));
replace: if !std::fs::symlink_metadata(&next).is_ok_and(|metadata| metadata.file_type().is_symlink()) { places.push(directory.join(&name)); }
packages: cineris-base
caught-by:
    cineris-base program::tests::a_link_into_or_out_of_an_avoided_root_is_passed_over

[break] shell-found-inside-a-write-root
rule: A shell on `PATH` inside the workspace or a write root is never chosen: the search goes on to the next.
file: crates/cineris-tools/src/shell/kind.rs
in: on_path
find: cineris_base::program::find_outside(&self.path, name, self.windows, &self.avoid)
replace: cineris_base::program::find(&self.path, name, self.windows)
packages: cineris-tools,cineris-core
caught-by:
    cineris-tools::it shell_search::a_shell_in_an_avoided_directory_is_not_chosen
    cineris-core assemble::tests::a_shell_inside_a_write_root_is_passed_over

[break] a-configured-shell-in-a-write-root-taken
